      "writtenOn": "2013-08-23T04:50:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure what the alternative is.  We can\u0027t, say, use the regular protection provided in this wrapper as first step - since it might fail because we havn\u0027t provided target entities that might be checked by the policy rule.  What this means is that unusual API calls that deal with multiple entities (e.g. check_grant()) do have to do something different.  It turns out that that this, so far, has only been needed in two classes of API call (see identity controller)",
